SlopWorld on Fedora
==================

As your normal user, attach the packaged mod to native Linux RimWorld 1.6:

  RIMWORLD=/path/to/RimWorld/game
  slopworld mod install --game "$RIMWORLD"
  systemctl --user daemon-reload
  systemctl --user enable --now slopd.service
  slopworld

The installer saves the game path and uses /usr/share/slopworld/SlopWorld.
Use --source DIR for another mod tree. Omit --game if RIMWORLD is exported
or the path is saved. Enable SlopWorld in the game's mod list.
After upgrading, run as your normal user:

  slopworld mod install
  systemctl --user daemon-reload
  systemctl --user try-restart slopd.service

Before removing the package, run as your normal user:

  systemctl --user disable --now slopd.service
  slopworld mod uninstall

After removal, run systemctl --user daemon-reload.
Configuration, sessions, and saves are preserved.
A source installation's unit under ~/.config/systemd/user overrides the packaged
unit; remove it before enabling this one.

Auto prefers the optional moor pager when installed, then falls back to bat,
less, or more. The required bat and less packages provide highlighting and paging
without moor. Explicit tools and custom commands remain available.

The required xclip package provides clipboard and PRIMARY selection on the game's
X11/XWayland desktop, including connections to remote daemons.

Optional integrations
---------------------

The Suggests field lists optional packages; install those for the features you use.

  moor                  Preferred pager; not currently in official Fedora repositories.
  highlight             Alternative syntax highlighter.
  python3-pygments      Alternative highlighter (pygmentize).
  glib2                 Desktop associations and launching (gio), portal access (gdbus).
  python3-gobject, gtk3
                        Full native Open With chooser, using Python and GTK 3.
  xdg-desktop-portal    Open With fallback; also requires a backend appropriate
                        to your desktop and OpenURI interface version 3 or newer.
  xsel                  Fallback to the required xclip tool.
  procps-ng             Fallback process inspection.

Spotify playback requires ncspot and Spotify Premium; song recognition requires
songrec. These are not provided by the official target distribution repositories;
install them separately if needed. The game must find songrec on its PATH, and
the daemon must find ncspot on its PATH.
